;; perform-does-not-typecheck-its-arguments, third pass (aggregates and
;; pointer-shaped parameters).  The primitive pass measured what an ordinary
;; call accepts between scalars and made `perform` agree; this pass did the
;; same for the shapes it left alone.  Each row of the table in
;; elab_effects.c's perform_arg_shape_mismatch is a call's verdict on one
;; program; this fixture is the perform side of one row.
;;
;; ptr<void> <- "hi".  A call rejects a cstr at a ptr<void> parameter (the
;; two are distinct pointer types to the checker); so does perform now.  A fn
;; value, nil, and a ptr<T> are the three things a call admits there, and
;; tests/fixtures/perform-arg-aggregate-and-pointer-shapes keeps them
;; compiling.
(defeffect P [h : ptr<void>] : int)
(defn work [] : int (perform (P "hi")))
(defn main [] : int
  (println (handle (work) (P [h] k) (resume k 1)))
  0)
